# Fleet roster — one agent Unix user per line (comments and blank lines ignored).
# Installed to /usr/local/share/agentic/fleet-agents by install-host-services.
#
# This is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for which agents the host scripts cover: kb-sync syncs the
# users listed here (and refuses to run without the file), agentic-monitor sweeps them (falling back
# to on-disk discovery — while alarming — if the file is missing), and agentic-divergence-check
# reconciles this list against the brain repos actually on disk and reports drift in EITHER
# direction. A roster the code derives coverage from is what makes "we added an agent and half the
# tooling never heard about it" impossible.
#
# You normally never edit this by hand: `provision-agent` appends the agent it provisions and
# refreshes the installed copy, then asks you to commit the change. Remove a line only when you
# decommission an agent (see runbooks/manage-agents.md) — the divergence check reports a stale
# entry either way.
